    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This two-bedroom semi-detached home offers excellent potential for buyers seeking to create a property tailored to their own tastes. Having been vacant for more than two years, the property may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to the applicable terms and eligibility criteria. A particular highlight is the exceptionally large south-facing rear garden, offering an abundance of outdoor space and excellent potential for landscaping, recreation or further enhancement.\n\nSituated in the heart of Cloghroe, St Senan's Terrace enjoys a convenient, well-established residential setting within easy reach of local schools, shops and everyday amenities. Regular bus services provide access to Cork City, while Blarney, Ballincollig and the surrounding areas are only a short drive away. Combining village living with excellent accessibility, this property represents an exciting opportunity for purchasers looking to make their mark and create a home of their own in a convenient location.\n\nHallway 1.65m x 1.08m\nA welcoming entrance hallway featuring a staircase to the first-floor accommodation.\nBright and spacious, with excellent potential to add your own personal touch.\n\nLiving Room- 2.85m x 4.80m\nA spacious living room with feature fireplace and excellent natural light, offering great potential for modernisation and refurbishment.\n\nKitchen & Dining K 2.41m x 2.77m & D 2.41m x 2.04m\nThe room includes an older fitted kitchen, stainless-steel sink and traditional brick fireplace, with a window providing natural light. While requiring significant upgrading throughout, the space offers good potential for a purchaser to redesign and create a modern kitchen/dining area.\n\nInternal Hall\nLeading to rear garden, plenty of understairs storage.\n\nStairs & Landing\nThe entrance hall provides access to the staircase leading to the first-floor landing, with a window at landing level providing natural light.\n\nBedroom 1 2.85m x 4.80m\nA generously proportioned bedroom with dual aspect windows providing good natural light. The room features a traditional fireplace and offers ample space for bedroom furniture.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.41m x 2.77m\nA well-proportioned second bedroom benefiting from two windows providing good natural light, together with a traditional fireplace. The room offers generous accommodation with excellent potential to create a bright and comfortable bedroom.\n\nBathroom WC & Store Room:\nTo the rear of the property is a separate WC and adjoining store room, both accessed externally from the rear yard. The WC is fitted with a toilet and wash-hand basin, while the separate store provides useful additional storage space.\n\nWorkshop -\nA substantial detached workshop offering generous and versatile additional space, with block-built walls, exposed roof timbers, concrete flooring and good natural light from two windows. Currently arranged as a workshop/storage area, the building offers excellent potential for a variety of uses, such as a home workshop, hobby room, studio, home office or additional storage, subject to any necessary planning permission and building regulations.\n\nGarden Details -\nFront\nThe property benefits from a generous concrete driveway providing ample off-street parking, together with gated side access leading to the rear of the property. The wide frontage and convenient side access are practical features offering easy access to the rear yard and outbuildings.\n\nRear\nOne of the standout features of the property is the exceptionally large rear garden, extending a considerable distance from the house and predominantly laid to lawn. Bordered by mature hedging and greenery, the garden offers an excellent sense of space and privacy, with significant potential for landscaping, outdoor living or further development, subject to the necessary planning permission. A particularly attractive feature for families, gardening enthusiasts or purchasers seeking generous outdoor space.\n\nFeatures\nTwo-bedroom semi-detached home with South facing rear garden\nExcellent refurbishment and modernisation potential\nOpportunity to create a home tailored to individual tastes\nVacant for more than two years\nMay qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to eligibility criteria\nConvenient location in Cloghroe, near Blarney\nClose to local schools, shops and everyday amenities\nRegular bus services to Cork City\nWithin easy driving distance of Blarney and Ballincollig\nIdeal opportunity for first-time buyers, families or investor\nInniscarra Community Centre is easily accessible\n\n\n"
      },
